{
  "name": "crf-default",
  "description": "Creative Ranges chord-card theme. `pitches` is the CRF pitch palette used when a surface's colorMode is \"pitch\"; `roots` is the per-root resolution used when it is \"single\". Every value is explicit — nothing is derived at load time, so what is written here is what prints. `titleHighlight` is white on every root: with the title's paint-order ink stroke carrying the edge, one consistent fill beats the earlier adaptive white/shade split (proofed 2026-08-09). `paper`, `contrast`, `groove` and `gradient` are the shared brand motifs (the 45 groove fingerprint and the root-colour sheen) that the chord library site and the cards both read; their rules are in this package's DESIGN.md.",
